1
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:20,938
Welcome, foolish mortals.

2
00:03:56,028 --> 00:03:57,571
It's love, isn't it?

3
00:03:57,696 --> 00:04:02,075
Sometimes you walk into a house,
take one look around, and you know.

4
00:04:02,201 --> 00:04:03,827
And you say, "This is for me."

5
00:04:03,952 --> 00:04:08,123
I think it's perfect.
It's just what we've been looking for.

6
00:04:09,208 --> 00:04:12,085
- There aren't enough plugs.
- Wait, Mr. Coleman.

7
00:04:12,211 --> 00:04:16,714
That place I showed you on
Sycamore Street was loaded with plugs.

8
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:18,800
That's right.
There were plenty.

9
00:04:18,884 --> 00:04:21,720
The steps were too high.
When we're old, we could trip.

10
00:04:21,845 --> 00:04:24,723
Every house we look at,
you find something to pick at.

11
00:04:24,848 --> 00:04:26,850
I just know what I like.

12
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:29,436
Would you like a divorce?
'Cause I'll bring it.

13
00:04:29,561 --> 00:04:32,022
Hey, no need for that.

14
00:04:32,147 --> 00:04:34,191
I'm gonna find this house for you.

15
00:04:34,316 --> 00:04:36,818
I'm committed to finding
your perfect house.

16
00:04:36,902 --> 00:04:40,364
I don't care how long it takes.
Because at Evers and Evers,

17
00:04:40,489 --> 00:04:44,159
we want you to be happy
forevers and evers.

18
00:04:44,243 --> 00:04:47,162
Let me take this call.

19
00:04:47,246 --> 00:04:50,541
So sorry. Evers and Evers Real Estate.
Jim Evers.

20
00:04:50,666 --> 00:04:53,377
Hey, honey, how's it going?
Do they like the house?

21
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:56,672
Yes, this house is still available.

22
00:04:56,755 --> 00:04:59,258
I knew it. I told you
they were lookie-loos.

23
00:04:59,383 --> 00:05:01,552
Another interested party.
Excuse me.

24
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:03,762
I'm on my way home
to get ready for dinner.

25
00:05:03,887 --> 00:05:06,974
- I'm looking forward to tonight.
- Are you pre-approved?

26
00:05:07,099 --> 00:05:09,935
Yeah. The reservation's at 7:00,
so don't be late.

27
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:11,687
7:00's perfect.

28
00:05:11,770 --> 00:05:14,731
Let's get together at 7:00
and go over your offer.

29
00:05:14,857 --> 00:05:17,317
- OK, honey, see you later.
- You see what you did?

30
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:18,944
We love the house.

31
00:05:20,779 --> 00:05:23,740
- We love it.
- Well, then, Mrs. Coleman,

32
00:05:23,824 --> 00:05:28,078
taking that into consideration,
there's only one thing left to do.

33
00:05:28,203 --> 00:05:30,622
Let's sign some papers.

34
00:05:32,875 --> 00:05:34,835
- Hey, Lorraine and Gary.
- Hi.

35
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:38,630
Just like I promised, here's the offer,
signed, sealed and delivered.

36
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:42,259
Thank you so much.
We are so grateful.

37
00:05:42,384 --> 00:05:45,345
This is a cause for celebration.
Let us buy you a drink.

38
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:48,182
No, I can't.
My wife's waiting for me.

39
00:05:48,307 --> 00:05:50,601
This is a big deal.
We have to celebrate.

40
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:52,186
- I really can't.
- We insist.

41
00:05:52,311 --> 00:05:53,770
Please.

42
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:57,024
OK, one quick drink.

43
00:05:57,149 --> 00:05:59,109
Sir, can I have a ginger ale, please?

44
00:05:59,234 --> 00:06:02,404
No, that's not a drink.
Sammy, three Volcanoes.

45
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:04,698
- No Volcanoes.
- Incredibly smooth.

46
00:06:04,823 --> 00:06:07,409
We love it here.
We've been coming here for years.

47
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:08,952
- It's like Hawaii.
- Yes.

48
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:12,206
- We spent our honeymoon there.
- It was fantastic. You been?

49
00:06:12,331 --> 00:06:14,082
- Never.
- Promise me you'll go.

50
00:06:14,166 --> 00:06:16,627
- Promise.
- I'll go if you sign,

51
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,462
but I got to get going now.

52
00:06:18,545 --> 00:06:21,298
It's my anniversary tonight.
I'm trying to get home.

53
00:06:21,423 --> 00:06:23,717
Your anniversary?
Happy anniversary!

54
00:06:23,842 --> 00:06:25,469
Thank you.
Sign the thing here.

55
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:28,889
Happy anniversary
Happy anniversary

56
00:06:29,014 --> 00:06:31,600
Happy anniversary
Happy anniversary

57
00:06:31,683 --> 00:06:33,977
- Happy, happy, happy...
- Hey, sign this!

58
00:06:35,521 --> 00:06:38,398
- OK, Jim.
- Sorry about that.

59
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:44,196
Pleasure doing business with you.
Aloha. OK? Bye-bye.

60
00:06:45,656 --> 00:06:47,616
Excuse me.
Did I hear you correctly?

61
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:50,327
- Did you just sell their house?
- I sure did.

62
00:06:50,452 --> 00:06:52,454
'Cause we're looking to buy.

63
00:06:57,042 --> 00:06:59,002
Honey, forgive me.

64
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:02,506
I'm Jim Evers
of Evers and Evers Real Estate.

65
00:07:02,631 --> 00:07:04,758
Tell me about
your dream house.

66
00:07:06,176 --> 00:07:09,972
Hi, Sara, my name's Teddy. Your husband
told me to tell you he loves you,

67
00:07:10,055 --> 00:07:13,976
but sometimes he loses track
of the time. I'm sorry I'm late.

68
00:07:14,726 --> 00:07:16,645
Happy anniversary!

69
00:07:16,728 --> 00:07:18,313
Happy anniversary.

70
00:07:18,397 --> 00:07:19,815
Yes.

71
00:07:21,233 --> 00:07:23,652
Look at what he brought you.

72
00:07:23,735 --> 00:07:25,445
Look at that.
Isn't that pretty?

73
00:07:25,571 --> 00:07:29,867
You have a wonderful husband that thinks
about you like that on your anniversary.

74
00:07:29,992 --> 00:07:32,828
- You're so fortunate.
- It's beautiful.

75
00:07:34,288 --> 00:07:38,417
It's actually Teddy's fault I'm late. He
had a little accident in the back seat.

76
00:07:38,542 --> 00:07:40,836
Cotton all over the place,
but I cleaned it up.

77
00:07:40,919 --> 00:07:44,089
It's OK.
I forgive Teddy.

78
00:07:44,214 --> 00:07:46,216
Come on, Sara.
Don't be like that.

79
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:49,261
I'm on a roll here.
We sold seven houses this month.

80
00:07:49,386 --> 00:07:53,390
What about the three soccer games,
two birthdays and barbecue you missed?

81
00:07:53,515 --> 00:07:55,517
Did I miss that much stuff
this month?

82
00:07:56,935 --> 00:07:59,313
OK, we're gonna take off
this weekend.

83
00:07:59,438 --> 00:08:01,356
- What?
- Take off for the weekend.

84
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,609
We'll go to the lake like last year.

85
00:08:03,734 --> 00:08:06,111
Just us and the kids.
How's that sound?

86
00:08:06,236 --> 00:08:07,529
Can we close on this?

87
00:08:07,613 --> 00:08:10,157
Yes. We can close on this.
How about this?

88
00:08:11,742 --> 00:08:15,287
Close on that.
Let me tell the kids. All right!

89
00:08:15,412 --> 00:08:18,081
Megan and Michael!
Big family adventure!

90
00:08:18,165 --> 00:08:20,250
Hey, Michael Jordan Evers!

91
00:08:21,793 --> 00:08:24,796
- Hey...
- Dad, there's a...

92
00:08:24,922 --> 00:08:27,090
- What is it?
- There's a spider in my room!

93
00:08:27,174 --> 00:08:29,301
- A what?
- A spider on the window.

94
00:08:29,426 --> 00:08:33,179
- Why don't you kill it, man?
- That's a big spider!

95
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:36,183
It's just a spider.
How big can it be?

96
00:08:36,308 --> 00:08:39,311
What is this?
Where's the spider at?

97
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:42,438
You're acting like it's Mothra.
It's just a spider.

98
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:44,733
You're making a big deal
out of nothing.

99
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:48,612
You're ten, and it's time I teach you
how to kill a spider the right way.

100
00:08:48,695 --> 00:08:50,822
The most efficient way
to crush a spider.

101
00:08:50,948 --> 00:08:53,534
Get a good magazine.
Doesn't matter what you use.

102
00:08:53,659 --> 00:08:56,870
Some people use Life
or Time or News...

103
00:08:58,872 --> 00:09:03,043
This is my Sports Illustrated Swimsuit
Edition. What are you doing with it?

104
00:09:03,168 --> 00:09:05,671
- I don't know.
- Yeah, right.

105
00:09:05,796 --> 00:09:10,050
If you can look at this, you should
have enough courage to kill a spider.

106
00:09:10,175 --> 00:09:12,135
Roll this up tight.
Get a good grip.

107
00:09:12,261 --> 00:09:14,638
Get a bead on the spider.
Gonna side swing.

108
00:09:14,763 --> 00:09:16,723
That's where you can
get good action.

109
00:09:16,849 --> 00:09:19,309
Come across like that
so you really crush it.

110
00:09:19,434 --> 00:09:23,438
You come across this way so you
get his whole escape route.

111
00:09:23,522 --> 00:09:26,817
You take it and you whack it.
Whack the spider.

112
00:09:26,942 --> 00:09:28,318
I don't want to whack it.

113
00:09:28,443 --> 00:09:30,654
You got to whack the spider, Mike.

114
00:09:30,779 --> 00:09:32,865
I'm afraid of spiders.
I can't whack it.

115
00:09:34,199 --> 00:09:36,535
Let me explain something to you.

116
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:38,996
All your life,
you'll be facing spiders. OK?

117
00:09:39,997 --> 00:09:40,998
I am?

118
00:09:41,123 --> 00:09:44,293
What I'm trying to say is
don't be afraid of anything.

119
00:09:44,376 --> 00:09:47,629
People use your fear against you.
I'm not scared of anything.

120
00:09:47,713 --> 00:09:50,382
I'm your dad, you're my son.
Whack that spider.

121
00:09:50,507 --> 00:09:51,717
I can't.

122
00:09:51,842 --> 00:09:54,261
You can do it.
Whack the spider.

123
00:09:54,386 --> 00:09:56,889
- I don't want to whack it.
- Yes, you can.

124
00:09:57,014 --> 00:09:58,640
- Kill the spider.
- I can't.

125
00:09:58,724 --> 00:10:01,602
Dad, I can't crush it.

126
00:10:02,269 --> 00:10:04,646
- Hey.
- There. Happy?

127
00:10:04,730 --> 00:10:07,482
No, Megan. I was trying to make
a point to your brother

128
00:10:07,566 --> 00:10:10,319
about how it's important
to whack your own spiders.

129
00:10:10,402 --> 00:10:12,196
Whatever.

130
00:10:12,905 --> 00:10:17,367
- ...past the Old Miller Road.
- OK, great.

131
00:10:17,451 --> 00:10:20,037
It is an old home, Ms. Evers,

132
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:23,457
and my employer
is anxious to move on.

133
00:10:23,582 --> 00:10:26,585
Would it be possible
for you to come alone

134
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:28,587
to discuss the situation?

135
00:10:28,712 --> 00:10:30,547
My husband and I work as a team.

136
00:10:30,631 --> 00:10:33,717
The master usually does not
take visitors.

137
00:10:33,842 --> 00:10:36,136
However, from your photograph,

138
00:10:36,261 --> 00:10:39,139
he thought you to have
a trustworthy face.

139
00:10:39,264 --> 00:10:42,726
About your husband,
he felt differently.

140
00:10:42,851 --> 00:10:45,062
You got our flyer.

141
00:10:45,187 --> 00:10:48,565
The master had wished
to meet you tomorrow evening.

142
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:52,277
I'm sorry, but tomorrow I've got plans
that can't be broken.

143
00:10:53,278 --> 00:10:55,280
- Excuse me a second.
- Who's that?

144
00:10:55,405 --> 00:10:57,950
Just someone calling
about repping a house.

145
00:10:58,075 --> 00:11:00,035
What's the address?
Where is it?

146
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:03,622
Sara! Do you know
where this place is?

147
00:11:03,747 --> 00:11:07,167
All the places up here
are multimillion-dollar mansions.

148
00:11:07,292 --> 00:11:09,920
What about our big family adventure?

149
00:11:10,963 --> 00:11:14,591
- It's just a little detour.
- How long is it gonna take?

150
00:11:14,716 --> 00:11:18,303
No more than 20 minutes.
You should be excited.

151
00:11:18,428 --> 00:11:21,223
You get to see Mommy and Daddy
in real estate action.

152
00:11:22,182 --> 00:11:23,809
Who's calling me?

153
00:11:25,185 --> 00:11:27,813
Jim Evers,
Evers and Evers Real Estate.

154
00:11:27,938 --> 00:11:30,190
Stan, how you doing?
What's the latest?

155
00:11:32,109 --> 00:11:35,571
Really? The Selmar property?
Tomorrow?

156
00:11:35,654 --> 00:11:37,990
I'm kind of out of town right now.

157
00:11:38,699 --> 00:11:42,411
But listen.
Maybe I could come back early.

158
00:11:42,494 --> 00:11:46,999
No, I can't come back early.

159
00:11:47,124 --> 00:11:50,627
Maybe we should take care of this
on Monday. All right? Monday?

160
00:11:50,711 --> 00:11:54,047
Monday sounds fantastic.
OK, I'll talk to you on Monday.

161
00:11:54,173 --> 00:11:55,883
Gonna talk on Monday.

162
00:11:59,261 --> 00:12:01,221
Are we still in America?

163
00:12:03,473 --> 00:12:06,643
Here it is, right here.
OK? All right?

164
00:12:17,321 --> 00:12:19,656
That's a whole lot of gate.

165
00:12:19,781 --> 00:12:22,826
They must have a big
possum problem down here.

166
00:12:23,535 --> 00:12:25,204
That's some big possum.

167
00:12:33,337 --> 00:12:36,006
- Didn't they know we were coming?
- Of course.

168
00:12:36,131 --> 00:12:38,217
Maybe there's a call box or something.

169
00:12:39,218 --> 00:12:40,385
Hello?

170
00:12:42,888 --> 00:12:44,973
Hello? The Evers are here!

171
00:12:48,519 --> 00:12:50,938
Yes, we're here now!

172
00:12:52,981 --> 00:12:54,775
Nobody's answering.

173
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:57,986
I gotta get out in the dirt
with my brand-new shoes on.

174
00:13:12,709 --> 00:13:14,127
Wow.

175
00:13:15,712 --> 00:13:17,339
How we gonna get in?

176
00:13:18,757 --> 00:13:21,468
Give me a boost.
I'll climb over and go around back.

177
00:13:21,593 --> 00:13:25,264
- Probably old. We'll surprise them.
- You'll probably kill 'em.

178
00:13:25,389 --> 00:13:28,141
Let's just go. It's getting late.

179
00:13:28,267 --> 00:13:30,769
You give up too easy.
You gotta be more patient.

180
00:13:30,894 --> 00:13:33,480
The Evers way is to be patient...

181
00:13:41,488 --> 00:13:43,365
All right.
We're in business.

182
00:13:43,448 --> 00:13:44,867
Let's go.

183
00:13:44,950 --> 00:13:46,577
Let's do this.

184
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:29,119
Bob Vila would have
a field day with this place.

185
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:33,040
Megan, don't slam the door like that.
It's very sensitive.

186
00:14:33,165 --> 00:14:35,209
It's a car, Dad.

187
00:14:35,334 --> 00:14:37,211
It's not just a car.

188
00:14:37,336 --> 00:14:39,463
It's a very delicate piece of machinery.

189
00:14:39,546 --> 00:14:42,841
She didn't mean what she just said.
She didn't mean that.

190
00:14:43,675 --> 00:14:45,719
Let's see what's around back.

191
00:14:45,844 --> 00:14:47,471
- I'm getting hungry.
- Me, too.

192
00:14:47,554 --> 00:14:49,765
Don't worry. We'll be 20 minutes, tops.

193
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:52,351
When we get to the lake,
can I go to that pizza shop

194
00:14:52,476 --> 00:14:55,979
where I ate that whole pizza, and when
we got to the cabin, I threw up,

195
00:14:56,104 --> 00:14:57,940
and you saw pepperoni chunks in it?

196
00:14:58,023 --> 00:15:02,236
- Can we go there?
- If we can avoid a repeat performance.

197
00:15:06,114 --> 00:15:09,117
Wow. That's something
you don't see every day.

198
00:15:09,201 --> 00:15:12,329
Oh, my God.

199
00:15:12,454 --> 00:15:14,164
Dead people?

200
00:15:14,248 --> 00:15:19,545
Hey, honey, you know they have
dead people in the backyard.

201
00:15:19,670 --> 00:15:24,758
Some people have pools, some people
have private cemeteries. It happens.

202
00:15:24,883 --> 00:15:27,886
You're gonna sell a house with this?

203
00:15:28,011 --> 00:15:31,223
This historical, sprawling manor
with spacious grounds? Yes.

204
00:15:31,348 --> 00:15:33,225
That's good.
Put that on the listing.

205
00:15:33,350 --> 00:15:37,229
- And leave out the dead people?
- Stick to the bright side.

206
00:15:37,354 --> 00:15:40,232
Oh, no. I got my good suit on.

207
00:15:46,446 --> 00:15:49,658
- You think it'll stop?
- I hope it's not raining at the lake.

208
00:15:51,159 --> 00:15:55,664
When you're at work with Mommy and
Daddy, you're on your best behavior.

209
00:15:57,291 --> 00:15:59,251
Look at the size of these knockers.

210
00:15:59,376 --> 00:16:01,336
Ever seen anything like that before?

211
00:16:02,296 --> 00:16:04,798
Hello! Evers Real Estate!

212
00:16:07,009 --> 00:16:09,052
Evers Real Estate.

213
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:23,192
Hello?

214
00:16:24,443 --> 00:16:26,445
Is anybody home?

215
00:16:30,866 --> 00:16:32,743
Hello.

216
00:16:32,868 --> 00:16:35,746
We're the Evers from
Evers and Evers Real Estate.

217
00:16:37,122 --> 00:16:38,749
Hi!

218
00:16:45,297 --> 00:16:47,466
Have you ever seen anything like this?

219
00:16:47,591 --> 00:16:50,928
Never. Sara, this puts us
in a whole new league.

220
00:16:52,262 --> 00:16:54,431
Smells like Grandma's house.

221
00:16:54,515 --> 00:16:56,558
Worse. Smells like Grandma.

222
00:16:56,642 --> 00:16:59,603
It's just dusty.
Get a cleaning crew to shine it up,

223
00:16:59,686 --> 00:17:02,314
this place will be sparkling
from top to bottom.

224
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:06,777
Mom, this place has spiders.

225
00:17:27,422 --> 00:17:29,967
Sara Evers?

226
00:17:30,092 --> 00:17:32,386
Yes. I'm Sara.

227
00:17:32,511 --> 00:17:35,973
My name is Ramsley.

228
00:17:39,977 --> 00:17:43,647
Hello, Ramsley. I'm Jim Evers
of Evers and Evers Real Estate.

229
00:17:43,772 --> 00:17:45,858
At your service.

230
00:17:46,692 --> 00:17:49,444
We were not expecting...

231
00:17:49,528 --> 00:17:50,821
others.

232
00:17:50,946 --> 00:17:53,490
Yes, we were on our way
out of town.

233
00:17:53,615 --> 00:17:58,370
Then when we realized the enormity
and complexity of your unique estate,

234
00:17:58,495 --> 00:18:01,665
we wanted to commit the full
resources of Evers and Evers,

235
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:04,668
because we want you to be happy
forevers and evers.

236
00:18:04,793 --> 00:18:09,381
Please accept this waterproof calendar
as a token of our appreciation.

237
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:16,471
Very well.
We shall have to place other settings.

238
00:18:16,555 --> 00:18:18,724
What are the other settings for?

239
00:18:18,849 --> 00:18:23,979
Master Gracey wishes to discuss
his affairs over dinner.

240
00:18:24,062 --> 00:18:26,231
I'm afraid we have plans.

241
00:18:26,356 --> 00:18:29,693
- Honey, we can't stay for dinner.
- We mustn't be rude, darling.

242
00:18:29,776 --> 00:18:32,362
- What about our family adventure?
- Yeah, Dad.

243
00:18:32,446 --> 00:18:35,949
We'll just have some soup
and get going. OK?

244
00:18:44,249 --> 00:18:45,542
Wow.

245
00:18:57,846 --> 00:18:59,473
Wow.

246
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:05,604
Nice. Very nice. Good job.

247
00:19:05,729 --> 00:19:08,148
Megan, how'd you like to eat
like this every day?

248
00:19:10,817 --> 00:19:13,820
The master will be with you shortly.

249
00:19:16,448 --> 00:19:17,491
Carry on.

250
00:19:23,455 --> 00:19:26,083
I said, "Carry on," and he walks off.

251
00:19:29,461 --> 00:19:33,966
Have you ever seen a fireplace
this amazing? Incredible.

252
00:19:34,091 --> 00:19:38,011
We could have one heck of
a wienie roast in that thing.

253
00:19:38,136 --> 00:19:42,599
Seriously. Look at this detail.
I've never seen anything like this.

254
00:19:42,724 --> 00:19:44,434
Haven't you?

255
00:19:45,936 --> 00:19:49,439
My grandfather spared no expense
when he built this mansion.

256
00:19:50,607 --> 00:19:53,151
Your grandfather had
good taste in tchotchkes.

257
00:19:53,277 --> 00:19:57,197
Jim Evers, Evers and Evers Real Estate.
Charmed to make your acquaintance.

258
00:19:57,322 --> 00:20:00,117
Edward. Edward Gracey.

259
00:20:06,582 --> 00:20:10,294
This is my wife.
Sara, you want to come meet Mr. Gracey?

260
00:20:10,377 --> 00:20:12,129
Very nice to meet you, Mr. Gracey.

261
00:20:12,254 --> 00:20:16,091
And this is our daughter, Megan,
and our son, Michael.

262
00:20:20,554 --> 00:20:23,223
You have very beautiful children,
Ms. Evers.

263
00:20:24,558 --> 00:20:27,477
I kicked in some chromosomes, too.

264
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:31,815
Children? Madame?

265
00:20:31,899 --> 00:20:35,444
Oh, nice. All right. OK.

266
00:20:38,655 --> 00:20:40,157
Thank you.

267
00:20:40,908 --> 00:20:42,534
The master was very pleased

268
00:20:42,659 --> 00:20:45,579
when he heard you could come
on such short notice.

269
00:20:46,288 --> 00:20:49,583
Normally, we would not have
called you here so abruptly,

270
00:20:49,708 --> 00:20:51,835
but we had no other choice.

271
00:20:51,919 --> 00:20:56,006
You got termites or something? Big house
like this must have a lot of termites.

272
00:20:56,131 --> 00:20:59,051
No, but lately
there have been more...

273
00:20:59,176 --> 00:21:01,094
disturbances.

274
00:21:02,554 --> 00:21:04,681
What do you think
of the house, Ms. Evers?

275
00:21:07,184 --> 00:21:09,269
I think it's absolutely incredible.

276
00:21:09,394 --> 00:21:12,856
The Italian influence,
the Renaissance style of the molding.

277
00:21:12,940 --> 00:21:15,651
The attention to detail is stunning.

278
00:21:15,734 --> 00:21:18,987
You never see houses like this.
Or, at least, I don't.

279
00:21:19,071 --> 00:21:22,741
Great care and love went into
the building of this mansion.

280
00:21:36,505 --> 00:21:41,176
This house is my inheritance,
my birthright.

281
00:21:42,719 --> 00:21:44,888
But lately it's become
too much to bear.

282
00:21:46,181 --> 00:21:48,225
Tell me, Mr. Evers.

283
00:21:48,308 --> 00:21:50,727
Do you believe in ghosts?

284
00:21:50,811 --> 00:21:52,729
Ghosts?

285
00:21:52,855 --> 00:21:55,274
Sure, I believe in ghosts.

286
00:21:55,399 --> 00:21:58,443
You don't want to put
that information on the listing.

287
00:21:58,569 --> 00:22:00,696
Talk about how many bathrooms
you have.

288
00:22:00,779 --> 00:22:03,365
People love bathrooms.
Play up the toilet angle.

289
00:22:03,448 --> 00:22:06,285
Leave out ghosts for now.
I think that'd be best.

290
00:22:07,077 --> 00:22:09,913
The storm has swollen the river.

291
00:22:09,997 --> 00:22:11,373
How's that?

292
00:22:11,456 --> 00:22:14,042
The storm has flooded the road.

293
00:22:15,210 --> 00:22:19,715
I'm afraid there will be
no leaving the mansion tonight.

294
00:22:19,798 --> 00:22:20,757
What?

295
00:22:20,883 --> 00:22:24,428
Of course, you are all more than welcome

296
00:22:24,553 --> 00:22:27,181
to spend the night here.

297
00:22:27,306 --> 00:22:31,143
No, I really don't think we should.
We've got plans.

298
00:22:31,268 --> 00:22:35,022
I'm afraid there's no other way.

299
00:22:35,147 --> 00:22:37,983
Ramsley will show you to your rooms.

300
00:22:52,372 --> 00:22:55,792
I believe the children will
be comfortable in this room.

301
00:22:58,337 --> 00:23:02,132
- Yeah, real homey.
- You'll be fine.

302
00:23:03,884 --> 00:23:07,679
When you flush the toilet,
see how quickly it refills.

303
00:23:07,804 --> 00:23:09,306
Night, Dad.

304
00:23:09,389 --> 00:23:10,641
Goodnight.

305
00:23:16,063 --> 00:23:20,359
I hope you and the madame will
find this room to your liking.

306
00:23:20,484 --> 00:23:24,196
Yeah, it's great. It'll be like
spending the night in a fine hotel.

307
00:23:24,321 --> 00:23:26,949
Will there be anything else
that you require, sir?

308
00:23:27,032 --> 00:23:29,451
- You gonna get us some chocolates?
- Pardon?

309
00:23:29,535 --> 00:23:31,912
The chocolates
they put on hotel pillows.

310
00:23:32,037 --> 00:23:35,666
Sometimes they have chocolates
on the pillow.

311
00:23:36,291 --> 00:23:37,793
They have...

312
00:23:39,169 --> 00:23:40,838
What's the problem?

313
00:23:45,092 --> 00:23:47,719
In the first place,
we weren't supposed to be here.

314
00:23:47,845 --> 00:23:51,807
- We were supposed to be at the lake.
- Am I supposed to control the weather?

315
00:23:51,890 --> 00:23:54,977
That's not the point.
You couldn't resist. You had to come.

316
00:23:55,060 --> 00:23:58,105
This is a big opportunity for all of us.

317
00:23:58,230 --> 00:24:00,357
Not for us. For you.

318
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:02,985
The only thing you seem
to care about is work.

319
00:24:03,068 --> 00:24:05,237
But when I work hard,
it doesn't matter

320
00:24:05,362 --> 00:24:08,657
as long as I'm bringing you home
expensive gifts, right?

321
00:24:10,158 --> 00:24:12,369
What are you... Sara.

322
00:24:12,494 --> 00:24:15,789
Sara, I didn't mean to say that. OK?

323
00:24:15,914 --> 00:24:19,042
Come on, stop. Sara?

324
00:24:19,168 --> 00:24:22,337
I'm sorry about that, honey.
Open up, please.

325
00:24:29,094 --> 00:24:30,721
You scared me.

326
00:24:30,804 --> 00:24:32,764
- Pardon the intrusion, sir.
- Yes?

327
00:24:32,890 --> 00:24:36,727
The master was wondering if he might
have a word with you in the library?

328
00:24:36,810 --> 00:24:39,438
A word? Yeah, I'd love
to have a word with him.

329
00:24:39,563 --> 00:24:42,941
- Let's go talk some turkey.
- Yes. Turkey.

330
00:24:43,066 --> 00:24:44,610
- Very good, sir.
- Yeah.

331
00:24:44,735 --> 00:24:47,404
If you will kindly follow me.

332
00:24:47,487 --> 00:24:51,325
Of course. Sara, I'm gonna have
a word with Mr. Gracey.

333
00:24:51,450 --> 00:24:53,744
I'll be back in a minute.

334
00:24:55,287 --> 00:24:59,875
You ever been to a tanning salon?
I've got a friend who's got a place.

335
00:24:59,958 --> 00:25:03,420
You can get a smooth tan,
do something about that ashy white look.

336
00:25:03,545 --> 00:25:07,132
Get a little bronze thing happening.
The ladies will love it.

337
00:25:07,257 --> 00:25:10,093
Yes, sounds wonderful.

338
00:25:12,513 --> 00:25:15,807
Would you care for a drink, sir,
while you're waiting?

339
00:25:15,933 --> 00:25:18,477
Yeah, don't mind if I do.
Thank you, Ramsley.

340
00:25:18,602 --> 00:25:20,062
Oh, wow.

341
00:25:20,145 --> 00:25:23,065
Now, that's class.
I need to do that over at my place.

342
00:25:23,148 --> 00:25:25,984
Get a big picture of myself
for the living room wall.

343
00:25:26,109 --> 00:25:28,070
Adds a touch of elegance to the room.

344
00:25:28,153 --> 00:25:29,530
Yes, sir.

345
00:25:29,655 --> 00:25:30,948
Very elegant.

346
00:25:31,865 --> 00:25:34,159
Thank you so much, Ramsley.

347
00:25:38,497 --> 00:25:41,667
- So how long you been a butler?
- A long time.

348
00:25:41,792 --> 00:25:44,169
What are the most important
qualifications,

349
00:25:44,294 --> 00:25:46,630
in case I need
to do some interviewing?

350
00:25:46,713 --> 00:25:49,091
Attending to every detail.

351
00:25:49,174 --> 00:25:51,593
Understanding priorities.

352
00:25:51,677 --> 00:25:55,597
And above all,
knowing one's place.

353
00:25:57,015 --> 00:25:58,976
What's your boss like to do?

354
00:25:59,059 --> 00:26:01,144
What floats his boat?

355
00:26:02,688 --> 00:26:06,483
The master likes a great many things.

356
00:26:06,567 --> 00:26:10,070
Art, literature, beauty.

357
00:26:10,195 --> 00:26:12,739
And all that stuff about ghosts.

358
00:26:12,865 --> 00:26:15,909
Did he get a bad clam
in his jambalaya one night?

359
00:26:16,034 --> 00:26:18,161
You don't believe in ghosts, sir?

360
00:26:18,245 --> 00:26:19,955
Absolutely not.

361
00:26:20,038 --> 00:26:23,876
The way I see it,
you only go around the track once.

362
00:26:24,001 --> 00:26:26,837
So you do it full out,
all the way around.

363
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:30,799
Mr. Evers, may I confide in you?

364
00:26:31,925 --> 00:26:33,343
Please do.

365
00:26:33,468 --> 00:26:35,304
The master is not well.

366
00:26:35,387 --> 00:26:39,057
He must leave this house, Mr. Evers.
He must move on.

367
00:26:39,183 --> 00:26:43,353
It is of the gravest importance,
I assure you.

368
00:26:43,437 --> 00:26:45,355
Or I fear...

369
00:26:45,439 --> 00:26:47,733
the very worst.

370
00:26:50,068 --> 00:26:53,322
I can't believe this.
Still no reception.

371
00:26:53,405 --> 00:26:55,532
We had to take that little detour.

372
00:26:55,616 --> 00:26:58,243
"20 minutes, tops." Yeah, right.

373
00:26:58,368 --> 00:27:00,245
Think it's gonna stop raining soon?

374
00:27:00,370 --> 00:27:03,457
How should I know?
I'm not the weatherman.

375
00:27:07,586 --> 00:27:09,046
Stogies.

376
00:27:10,464 --> 00:27:14,092
Not bad.
Better hold on to that.

377
00:27:19,598 --> 00:27:22,392
Wonderful. Must be nice.

378
00:27:22,476 --> 00:27:25,145
Must be real nice. I tell you.

379
00:27:34,363 --> 00:27:37,199
Hello, good man.
Ramsley, fix the gentleman a drink.

380
00:27:37,282 --> 00:27:39,910
Nigel, I recently returned
from the continent,

381
00:27:39,993 --> 00:27:44,122
where I found the most interesting book.
It was called Raising the Dead...

382
00:27:44,248 --> 00:27:45,832
Oh, craps.

383
00:27:46,625 --> 00:27:48,710
I hope that doesn't stain.

384
00:28:00,889 --> 00:28:02,182
Wow.

385
00:28:17,406 --> 00:28:19,575
Interesting.

386
00:28:35,507 --> 00:28:37,801
I wonder where this leads to.

387
00:28:41,346 --> 00:28:43,307
Hey, open this back up!

388
00:28:43,432 --> 00:28:46,602
Open up! Ramsley!

389
00:28:47,853 --> 00:28:50,814
Ramsley! Push back the head!

390
00:28:52,691 --> 00:28:55,152
Can somebody push the head back?

391
00:29:28,477 --> 00:29:29,478
Megan!

392
00:29:35,776 --> 00:29:37,945
What do you think it is?

393
00:29:41,990 --> 00:29:44,034
It's a ghost ball.

394
00:29:59,925 --> 00:30:01,885
I think it wants us to follow it.

395
00:30:04,054 --> 00:30:06,223
I think you're crazy.

396
00:30:12,938 --> 00:30:15,732
It does.
It wants us to follow it.

397
00:30:31,248 --> 00:30:32,916
Hey, Megan, wait up.

398
00:30:39,256 --> 00:30:42,342
Where's that scary albino
when you need him?

399
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:50,434
Hello.

400
00:30:52,144 --> 00:30:55,105
Have you seen my husband?

401
00:30:59,109 --> 00:31:00,652
Excuse me.

402
00:31:02,279 --> 00:31:05,699
Wait. Wait.

403
00:31:24,551 --> 00:31:28,180
- Oh, Ramsley. It's you.
- May I help you?

404
00:31:28,305 --> 00:31:31,141
Yes, I was just looking
for my husband.

405
00:31:31,266 --> 00:31:32,809
Indeed.

406
00:31:32,935 --> 00:31:36,146
I left him in the library.

407
00:31:36,271 --> 00:31:38,732
Right through there.

408
00:31:40,901 --> 00:31:45,572
Honey, it's late.
Let's not fight anymore. Come to bed?

409
00:31:45,697 --> 00:31:47,658
I'm... sorry.

410
00:31:47,741 --> 00:31:50,702
- I thought you were my husband.
- Can I help you with that?

411
00:31:50,827 --> 00:31:53,664
Ramsley hates it when
I leave things lying about.

412
00:31:53,747 --> 00:31:55,916
Yes, he seems a bit proper.

413
00:31:56,041 --> 00:31:57,960
He strikes most people that way.

414
00:31:58,043 --> 00:32:01,505
Once you get to know him,
you'll find that's not the case.

415
00:32:01,588 --> 00:32:03,215
He's really...

416
00:32:04,633 --> 00:32:06,468
He's really very sweet.

417
00:32:07,261 --> 00:32:08,846
Thank you.

418
00:32:08,929 --> 00:32:10,889
He's been like a father to me.

419
00:32:11,014 --> 00:32:14,184
Mr. Gracey?
May I ask you something?

420
00:32:14,309 --> 00:32:17,145
Yes, of course. Anything.

421
00:32:17,229 --> 00:32:21,191
This house, it's been
in your family for generations.

422
00:32:21,316 --> 00:32:23,151
It's your home.

423
00:32:23,235 --> 00:32:25,487
Why do you want to sell it?

424
00:32:27,906 --> 00:32:30,325
These walls are filled...

425
00:32:30,409 --> 00:32:32,703
with so many memories.

426
00:32:32,828 --> 00:32:35,998
Some of them... painful.

427
00:32:39,251 --> 00:32:43,046
I think for you to understand,
I really must show you.

428
00:32:43,130 --> 00:32:45,090
It's all right.

429
00:32:45,215 --> 00:32:47,426
There's nothing to be afraid of.

430
00:32:51,763 --> 00:32:55,559
Although it might be a bit worn
and faded from its original grandeur,

431
00:32:55,684 --> 00:32:58,604
this house was once filled
with so many things.

432
00:32:58,729 --> 00:33:00,397
So much life.

433
00:33:00,480 --> 00:33:02,816
Grand parties, dancing, laughter,

434
00:33:02,941 --> 00:33:05,569
and above all, hope.

435
00:33:05,694 --> 00:33:08,906
Being a Gracey meant
that you were denied nothing.

436
00:33:08,989 --> 00:33:12,701
- The world was yours.
- What happened here, Mr. Gracey?

437
00:33:13,702 --> 00:33:16,371
- She did.
- Who?

438
00:33:16,455 --> 00:33:18,749
Elizabeth.

439
00:33:18,874 --> 00:33:22,002
Hers is the story
that haunts these walls.

440
00:33:47,778 --> 00:33:50,697
- Come on.
- Megan, wait.

441
00:33:51,782 --> 00:33:54,243
Don't know the last time
that's been inspected.

442
00:33:54,326 --> 00:33:57,579
Would you relax?
Where's your sense of adventure?

443
00:34:09,424 --> 00:34:11,510
This is against all my better judgment.

444
00:34:44,710 --> 00:34:46,837
Hi!

445
00:34:51,466 --> 00:34:53,635
Is anyone home?

446
00:35:13,197 --> 00:35:15,282
This must be termites.

447
00:35:18,035 --> 00:35:20,579
Some big ass termites, that's all.

448
00:36:18,804 --> 00:36:20,597
Hello?

449
00:37:14,860 --> 00:37:16,653
Megan!

450
00:37:22,451 --> 00:37:24,494
Mom.

451
00:37:24,578 --> 00:37:27,247
What are you doing?
You're not supposed to be here.

452
00:37:27,372 --> 00:37:29,833
This is unspeakable!
You have to leave!

453
00:37:29,958 --> 00:37:31,376
Who is that?

454
00:37:31,502 --> 00:37:33,754
None of your business.
Get out of here.

455
00:37:33,879 --> 00:37:36,423
- Way past your bedtime.
- Her name was Elizabeth!

456
00:37:36,548 --> 00:37:38,759
Are you kids hungry?
Anybody want a cookie?

457
00:37:38,884 --> 00:37:40,052
Cookies?

458
00:37:40,177 --> 00:37:43,055
Don't offer them cookies!
They're trespassers!

459
00:37:43,180 --> 00:37:46,475
Trespassers don't get cookies!
This is none of their concern.

460
00:37:46,558 --> 00:37:49,353
It is their concern.
They're involved!

461
00:37:50,479 --> 00:37:52,523
Hide. Hide!

462
00:38:04,159 --> 00:38:08,914
The children are not in their room.
Have you seen them?

463
00:38:09,039 --> 00:38:10,749
Children? What children?

464
00:38:10,874 --> 00:38:12,751
What children?

465
00:38:19,007 --> 00:38:20,884
Her children.

466
00:38:20,968 --> 00:38:24,346
The children
she wasn't supposed to bring,

467
00:38:24,429 --> 00:38:27,391
along with that
brainless husband of hers.

468
00:38:28,767 --> 00:38:29,935
Thank you.

469
00:38:38,110 --> 00:38:41,697
If I had to listen to another word
from that insufferable fool,

470
00:38:41,780 --> 00:38:43,615
I think I would've burst.

471
00:38:43,740 --> 00:38:46,785
Of course, sir. What a fool!

472
00:38:46,910 --> 00:38:49,538
Did I not tell her to come alone?

473
00:38:49,621 --> 00:38:52,165
Is it too much to ask
for a little cooperation,

474
00:38:52,291 --> 00:38:55,419
- a little order?
- Of course not, sir.

475
00:38:55,544 --> 00:38:57,838
If you find the children,

476
00:38:57,963 --> 00:38:59,756
bring them to me.

477
00:38:59,882 --> 00:39:01,258
Certainly, sir.

478
00:39:01,383 --> 00:39:03,886
The final arrangements
have been made.

479
00:39:03,969 --> 00:39:08,140
Nothing further will interfere
with the master's plan.

480
00:39:18,150 --> 00:39:23,071
Thank God I heard your voice. I'm lost.
I don't know how to get out of here.

481
00:39:23,155 --> 00:39:27,534
I'm sorry if I sound a little frazzled,
but I had a freak show back there.

482
00:39:29,494 --> 00:39:33,123
I was supposed to meet with Mr. Gracey,
but I got stuck in the wall.

483
00:39:33,248 --> 00:39:37,002
Goblins and ghoulies
from last Halloween,

484
00:39:37,127 --> 00:39:40,214
awaken the spirits
with your tambourine.

485
00:39:40,923 --> 00:39:43,675
OK, I hear you, but I don't see you.
Where are you?

486
00:39:43,800 --> 00:39:47,596
I am Madame Leota, seer of all.

487
00:39:47,679 --> 00:39:51,350
Voice to the spirits.
Whom do you seek?

488
00:39:56,313 --> 00:39:59,942
- What are you doing? Let me out!
- Silence! Whom do you seek?

489
00:40:00,025 --> 00:40:03,529
- I am seeking a way out.
- Then you must look within.

490
00:40:03,654 --> 00:40:07,115
- I don't want to. Are you deaf?
- There is great evil in this house.

491
00:40:07,199 --> 00:40:10,202
A devil's curse.
It seeks to destroy you.

492
00:40:10,327 --> 00:40:12,996
Why? I'm just here
to sell the house, OK?

493
00:40:13,121 --> 00:40:16,500
Dark spirits from the grave,
come forth.

494
00:40:16,583 --> 00:40:18,377
Lift us from the black,

495
00:40:18,502 --> 00:40:21,797
and show us,
show us the way back.

496
00:40:21,880 --> 00:40:25,092
Dark spirits? Don't you make
no dark spirits come out.

497
00:40:25,217 --> 00:40:28,011
Lift us, lift us up to the light,

498
00:40:28,095 --> 00:40:31,056
and lead us through
this stormy night.

499
00:40:33,559 --> 00:40:35,978
Hey, I'd really like
to stay on the ground.

500
00:40:36,061 --> 00:40:38,021
Can I stay on the ground, please?

501
00:40:38,146 --> 00:40:40,941
Evil and darkness
have fallen this night,

502
00:40:41,066 --> 00:40:44,361
but now to survive,
you must gain new sight.

503
00:40:44,486 --> 00:40:48,407
- I must first gain new underwear.
- Only the light could lead the way.

504
00:40:48,532 --> 00:40:50,951
Follow it and find your way home.

505
00:40:51,076 --> 00:40:54,454
There's no place like home.
There's no place like home.

506
00:40:54,580 --> 00:40:57,291
Go, Mr. Evers!
Your family is at stake.

507
00:40:57,416 --> 00:41:00,502
Your very life is at stake.
Break the curse!

508
00:41:00,586 --> 00:41:03,714
There is no escape for you
unless you lift the spell.

509
00:41:03,839 --> 00:41:05,716
Go. Save yourself!

510
00:41:05,799 --> 00:41:10,262
Save your family.
Release her. Release us all!

511
00:41:10,387 --> 00:41:13,140
I'm getting so queasy.
I'm getting very queasy.

512
00:42:06,860 --> 00:42:10,072
- Dad!
- Michael, Megan! You OK?

513
00:42:10,155 --> 00:42:12,950
- We're fine. Thanks.
- Get your things. Let's get out.

514
00:42:13,075 --> 00:42:15,077
- We have a problem.
- What? The rain?

515
00:42:15,160 --> 00:42:18,121
We'll just get wet.
Let's find your mom and get out!

516
00:42:18,247 --> 00:42:20,791
I'm afraid that's not possible.
She can't leave.

517
00:42:20,916 --> 00:42:22,876
- Why not?
- Because she can't.

518
00:42:23,001 --> 00:42:26,380
If I could tell you, I would.
But I can't, so I won't. OK?

519
00:42:26,505 --> 00:42:28,173
How'd you...

520
00:42:28,966 --> 00:42:32,094
Look, Daddy's having hallucinations.
Let's go, right now.

521
00:42:32,177 --> 00:42:33,887
- They're ghosts.
- They are not.

522
00:42:34,012 --> 00:42:36,473
We're having hallucinations
from that dinner.

523
00:42:36,598 --> 00:42:38,642
That chicken didn't taste right.

524
00:42:39,351 --> 00:42:41,311
- It's not the chicken!
- All right.

525
00:42:41,395 --> 00:42:43,856
- But we're still going.
- We have to help them.

526
00:42:43,981 --> 00:42:47,025
Can't help the dead.
They're beyond help. Nature of death.

527
00:42:47,150 --> 00:42:50,821
Everyone should keep
their noses in their own business.

528
00:42:50,946 --> 00:42:52,781
We have to help them break the curse.

529
00:42:52,865 --> 00:42:58,161
You been talking to that crazy green
gypsy in the giant paperweight?

530
00:42:58,287 --> 00:43:00,372
He found the gypsy!
We've got to go back!

531
00:43:00,497 --> 00:43:01,623
I'm not going back!

532
00:43:01,707 --> 00:43:04,001
- But, Dad...
- They had me floating around!

533
00:43:04,877 --> 00:43:08,005
I was strapped to a chair
with a marching band chasing me.

534
00:43:08,130 --> 00:43:11,383
- I'm not going back. Forget it, Casper!
- But Mom's in trouble.

535
00:43:11,508 --> 00:43:13,760
What kind of trouble?

536
00:43:26,690 --> 00:43:30,360
She died here, in this house.

537
00:43:31,069 --> 00:43:33,488
She was so very young,

538
00:43:33,572 --> 00:43:35,824
so very beautiful.

539
00:43:37,075 --> 00:43:40,871
She was in love
with the heir to this mansion.

540
00:43:40,996 --> 00:43:42,956
Your grandfather?

541
00:43:43,081 --> 00:43:47,085
And he loved her
more than life itself.

542
00:43:48,378 --> 00:43:50,797
But they were
from different worlds...

543
00:43:52,174 --> 00:43:54,384
and couldn't be together.

544
00:43:56,887 --> 00:43:58,972
How did she die, Mr. Gracey?

545
00:43:59,097 --> 00:44:02,893
She took her own life. Poison.

546
00:44:03,018 --> 00:44:07,564
After that, his life became unbearable.

547
00:44:07,689 --> 00:44:10,567
And so, without hope,

548
00:44:10,651 --> 00:44:12,569
without love,

549
00:44:12,694 --> 00:44:17,157
without Elizabeth...
he hung himself.

550
00:44:19,743 --> 00:44:23,163
His soul wanders these halls,

551
00:44:23,288 --> 00:44:25,958
waiting for her to return.

552
00:44:29,127 --> 00:44:32,130
If you listen carefully,

553
00:44:32,256 --> 00:44:37,177
you can still hear the beating
of his broken heart.

554
00:44:46,979 --> 00:44:50,065
Wait a minute. Hold it.
This guy is dead,

555
00:44:50,148 --> 00:44:53,443
and we were brought here 'cause
he wants to get jiggy with my wife?

556
00:44:53,569 --> 00:44:56,029
Pretty much. Are you upset?

557
00:44:56,154 --> 00:44:58,866
The guy is dead, and he's trying
to get with my wife!

558
00:44:58,991 --> 00:45:02,619
And the house isn't really for sale?
Yes, I'm upset.

559
00:45:02,744 --> 00:45:05,706
Oh, Madame Leota, is it her?

560
00:45:05,831 --> 00:45:09,626
Is she truly our dear, departed
Elizabeth come back to us?

561
00:45:09,710 --> 00:45:12,671
It is true.
She walks these halls.

562
00:45:12,796 --> 00:45:15,215
See, I told you. It is her.

563
00:45:15,340 --> 00:45:17,134
But do not be deceived.

564
00:45:17,217 --> 00:45:19,761
All things are not as they appear.

565
00:45:19,845 --> 00:45:23,098
For the curse to be lifted,
the truth must be known,

566
00:45:23,182 --> 00:45:26,351
and for the truth to be known,
you must find the key.

567
00:45:26,476 --> 00:45:28,979
What are you talking about,
ball lady? What key?

568
00:45:29,062 --> 00:45:31,273
Enter the tomb
under the great dead oak

569
00:45:31,356 --> 00:45:34,067
and travel down deep
under the ground,

570
00:45:34,193 --> 00:45:37,237
and there you will find
the key that must be found.

571
00:45:37,362 --> 00:45:40,157
Find the black crypt
that bears no name,

572
00:45:40,282 --> 00:45:43,035
or soon your fate will be the same.

573
00:45:43,160 --> 00:45:47,039
I find this key and I'll walk out with
my wife and kids like nothing happened?

574
00:45:47,164 --> 00:45:50,209
The key is the answer to all.

575
00:45:50,334 --> 00:45:52,127
I'm in. Let's get this key.

576
00:45:52,211 --> 00:45:55,756
There's only one problem.
How do we get out of here?

577
00:45:55,881 --> 00:45:58,008
Yeah, how do we get out of here?

578
00:45:58,133 --> 00:46:01,512
Well, there's always...

579
00:46:01,637 --> 00:46:03,472
my way.

580
00:46:10,896 --> 00:46:14,608
- You said you could drive this thing!
- Don't worry. I know what I'm doing.

581
00:46:21,073 --> 00:46:22,699
Keep your eyes on the road.

582
00:46:22,824 --> 00:46:24,493
- Move over!
- What are you doing?

583
00:46:24,576 --> 00:46:28,121
- You keep driving, you'll kill us all.
- That's where you're wrong,

584
00:46:28,247 --> 00:46:30,499
because some of us are already dead!

585
00:46:35,254 --> 00:46:36,547
Dad, look.

586
00:46:54,565 --> 00:46:56,775
Ready? Fire.

587
00:47:12,958 --> 00:47:15,127
- Dad?
- Yeah, son?

588
00:47:15,252 --> 00:47:17,713
I see dead people.

589
00:47:23,927 --> 00:47:27,264
Excuse me. Why are all these ghosts
still hanging around here?

590
00:47:27,389 --> 00:47:33,270
When they died, they couldn't find the
light. And now... now they're trapped.

591
00:47:33,353 --> 00:47:37,274
Doomed to wander the earth
for all eternity.

592
00:47:41,153 --> 00:47:43,530
Nice. Nice job.

593
00:48:00,005 --> 00:48:01,381
OK.

594
00:48:01,507 --> 00:48:03,717
Hey! What are you doing here?

595
00:48:04,760 --> 00:48:07,888
- Can they see us?
- No, of course not.

596
00:48:08,013 --> 00:48:10,807
Yes, I can. I'm looking at you
in your stupid hat.

597
00:48:10,933 --> 00:48:13,352
Don't listen to him.
He's lying.

598
00:48:14,645 --> 00:48:17,231
Whatever.
Come on, kids. Let's go.

599
00:48:18,690 --> 00:48:22,486
I could swear he was
looking right at me.

600
00:48:22,569 --> 00:48:24,696
He's psychic.

601
00:48:28,867 --> 00:48:31,828
This was to have been
her wedding dress.

602
00:48:31,954 --> 00:48:33,413
It's lovely.

603
00:48:33,539 --> 00:48:37,960
It would have been lovelier still
if she'd ever had a chance to wear it.

604
00:48:38,043 --> 00:48:43,632
Now it serves only as a dark reminder
of what could have been.

605
00:48:43,715 --> 00:48:46,844
To love someone so much
and lose them so suddenly.

606
00:48:46,969 --> 00:48:49,847
I can't imagine
how awful that must be.

607
00:48:49,972 --> 00:48:52,850
If you truly love someone,
they never leave you.

608
00:48:52,933 --> 00:48:56,019
They remain in your heart forever.

609
00:48:59,273 --> 00:49:00,983
Isn't that romantic?

610
00:49:01,066 --> 00:49:03,610
He was willing to throw
everything away for love.

611
00:49:03,735 --> 00:49:06,238
Now he's broke, dead, and cursed.
Nice move.

612
00:49:08,031 --> 00:49:11,869
Crap. These are my new shoes.
Kids, watch your step.

613
00:49:11,994 --> 00:49:13,036
Crap!

614
00:49:13,120 --> 00:49:14,746
Michael, don't say "crap."

615
00:49:14,872 --> 00:49:17,040
Where is this place?
Where are we?

616
00:49:17,165 --> 00:49:20,586
The gypsy lady said something
about making a left at an oak.

617
00:49:20,711 --> 00:49:23,881
OK. Glad she was so specific.

618
00:49:29,178 --> 00:49:31,597
What is that?
You hear that?

619
00:49:31,722 --> 00:49:33,182
Yeah.

620
00:49:35,559 --> 00:49:39,229
Grin grinning ghosts
Come out to socialize

621
00:49:40,939 --> 00:49:43,400
When the crypt goes creak
And the tombstones quake

622
00:49:43,525 --> 00:49:45,444
Spooks come out
For a swinging wake...

623
00:49:45,569 --> 00:49:47,404
Excuse me. Sorry to bother you.

624
00:49:47,529 --> 00:49:50,199
I was wondering if you know
where the mausoleum was.

625
00:49:50,282 --> 00:49:55,370
Down by
The old mill stream

626
00:49:55,454 --> 00:49:58,081
Where I first met...

627
00:49:58,207 --> 00:50:01,084
No, I think they said
it was an old oak?

628
00:50:01,210 --> 00:50:02,920
That's what they said.
It's by...

629
00:50:03,045 --> 00:50:05,339
- By the light
- By the light

630
00:50:05,464 --> 00:50:08,091
Of the silvery moon
Of the silvery moon...

631
00:50:08,175 --> 00:50:10,552
Guys, you sound good,
your harmony's tight.

632
00:50:10,636 --> 00:50:12,804
We're trying to find my wife.
She'll be...

633
00:50:12,930 --> 00:50:15,766
Comin' 'round the mountain
When she comes, when she comes

634
00:50:15,891 --> 00:50:18,352
She'll be comin' 'round
The mountain when she...

635
00:50:18,477 --> 00:50:20,437
I'm trying to find a key...

636
00:50:20,562 --> 00:50:23,106
Where's the key
Where's the key

637
00:50:23,232 --> 00:50:25,859
Where's the beautiful key?
Find the key, find the key

638
00:50:25,984 --> 00:50:27,444
Oh, how happy you'll be

639
00:50:27,528 --> 00:50:30,072
The key I'm trying to find
is in the mausoleum?

640
00:50:30,155 --> 00:50:31,949
The key is in the mausoleum!

641
00:50:32,074 --> 00:50:34,826
You left your key

642
00:50:34,952 --> 00:50:37,538
In a mausoleum

643
00:50:37,663 --> 00:50:40,624
- Down in Dixie
- Dad, there it is!

644
00:50:40,749 --> 00:50:42,626
- Dad, there it is
- Oh, thanks.

645
00:50:42,709 --> 00:50:47,089
- Dad, there it is
- Thanks for nothing.

646
00:50:51,552 --> 00:50:53,303
OK, we made it.

647
00:50:57,516 --> 00:50:59,768
All right, kids. Stay close.

648
00:51:13,866 --> 00:51:17,119
Look. It's a warning.

649
00:51:18,203 --> 00:51:22,207
- Now, how do you know that?
- I studied Latin for three years, Dad.

650
00:51:22,332 --> 00:51:25,752
You thought it was dumb, remember?
You said it was a dead language.

651
00:51:25,878 --> 00:51:29,006
Well, we see how wrong
I was about that.

652
00:51:29,131 --> 00:51:32,009
"Beware all who enter.

653
00:51:32,092 --> 00:51:36,180
Here lies the passage
to the dead."

654
00:51:37,055 --> 00:51:39,349
Hey! Where you going?

655
00:51:39,433 --> 00:51:42,019
- I don't like Latin.
- We've been through this.

656
00:51:42,144 --> 00:51:44,188
You're ten. Start being a man.

657
00:51:44,313 --> 00:51:47,316
I just turned ten.
I'm still getting used to it.

658
00:51:50,861 --> 00:51:51,945
Here's what we do.

659
00:51:52,070 --> 00:51:54,615
- Megan, stay with your brother.
- What?

660
00:51:54,740 --> 00:51:56,992
I'm not gonna leave him here
by himself.

661
00:51:57,075 --> 00:52:00,579
You guys stay together,
and I'll take care of this.

662
00:52:02,372 --> 00:52:04,333
All right.

663
00:52:25,729 --> 00:52:28,482
OK. All right.

664
00:52:32,277 --> 00:52:33,654
OK.

665
00:52:33,779 --> 00:52:35,072
I'll be right back.

666
00:52:35,155 --> 00:52:37,032
20 minutes, tops, right?

667
00:52:37,115 --> 00:52:39,201
20 minutes, tops.

668
00:53:21,869 --> 00:53:24,830
What was it that gypsy
told me to look for?

669
00:53:24,955 --> 00:53:26,707
Look for a crypt with...

670
00:53:28,000 --> 00:53:30,043
Look for a crypt...

671
00:53:30,169 --> 00:53:32,212
A crypt with no name.

672
00:53:32,337 --> 00:53:34,965
What's the matter with you?
You can't pop out.

673
00:53:35,090 --> 00:53:38,385
You'll give me a heart attack.
I told you to wait with Michael.

674
00:53:38,510 --> 00:53:40,929
I was worried you wouldn't find it.

675
00:53:41,013 --> 00:53:43,724
Besides, Michael's fine.

676
00:53:43,849 --> 00:53:46,560
She said, "Find the black crypt
with no name,

677
00:53:46,685 --> 00:53:48,729
"or soon your fate
will be the same."

678
00:53:55,777 --> 00:53:58,989
- That must be it.
- Good hunch, Dad.

679
00:54:02,326 --> 00:54:05,329
I'm officially starting
to get sick of this place.

680
00:54:05,454 --> 00:54:07,289
And we're here 'cause of who?

681
00:54:07,372 --> 00:54:10,584
Because I take seriously
my responsibility as breadwinner,

682
00:54:10,709 --> 00:54:13,045
and want you to have everything
I never had.

683
00:54:13,170 --> 00:54:15,881
- I didn't know you had a bad childhood.
- I didn't.

684
00:54:16,006 --> 00:54:18,509
Then why do we have to have
what you didn't have?

685
00:54:18,592 --> 00:54:19,718
Because...

686
00:54:19,843 --> 00:54:24,097
Don't be tricking me, you little
Latin-speaking 13-year-old.

687
00:54:24,223 --> 00:54:27,267
Let's just get this over with.
Hold this.

688
00:54:27,392 --> 00:54:29,269
Two hands, now.

689
00:54:48,247 --> 00:54:49,748
Oh, man!

690
00:54:52,167 --> 00:54:55,796
Excuse me. One second.
Sorry to bother you.

691
00:55:11,979 --> 00:55:13,939
OK. All right.

692
00:55:14,064 --> 00:55:17,734
That wasn't that hard, was it?
Let's get out of here.

693
00:55:20,654 --> 00:55:23,574
That gypsy had me thinking it'd be hard.
That was easy.

694
00:55:35,961 --> 00:55:38,213
Get the key!
I'll take care of him.

695
00:55:41,466 --> 00:55:43,552
Go on back to bed.
Get back in the bed.

696
00:55:44,970 --> 00:55:47,264
I'm Jim Evers
of Evers and Evers Real Estate.

697
00:55:47,389 --> 00:55:51,059
I don't want no trouble. Gypsy told me
it was all right to get the key...

698
00:55:53,478 --> 00:55:57,191
Lighten up. I'm trying to get the key
'cause I gotta get my wife.

699
00:55:57,316 --> 00:55:59,109
I don't want trouble!

700
00:55:59,234 --> 00:56:00,444
Back up!

701
00:56:04,740 --> 00:56:06,533
You asked for it.

702
00:56:10,370 --> 00:56:14,124
Next time, you'll think twice before
coming back from the dead, ain't you?

703
00:56:14,249 --> 00:56:17,336
- Did you get the key?
- I'm looking.

704
00:56:17,461 --> 00:56:20,547
Take your time. Relax.
I have everything under control.

705
00:56:20,672 --> 00:56:23,175
I have everything
completely under control.

706
00:56:27,679 --> 00:56:29,389
Megan, you better look faster!

707
00:56:29,515 --> 00:56:31,600
I don't want to do this.

708
00:57:27,322 --> 00:57:29,199
Give me your hand.

709
00:57:33,662 --> 00:57:35,205
Come on, come on!

710
00:57:37,749 --> 00:57:39,793
Come on! Hurry up!

711
00:57:39,918 --> 00:57:42,004
- Hold on! We're coming!
- Hurry!

712
00:57:43,797 --> 00:57:47,634
Michael, open the door!
It's locked from the outside!

713
00:57:47,759 --> 00:57:50,929
Michael, open the door.
Open the door!

714
00:57:51,054 --> 00:57:53,932
There are spiders everywhere.
I don't have a magazine!

715
00:57:54,057 --> 00:57:55,976
Michael, are you scared?

716
00:57:56,101 --> 00:57:58,937
It's OK to be scared.
Everybody gets scared.

717
00:57:59,062 --> 00:58:01,231
- Daddy's scared right now.
- You are?

718
00:58:01,356 --> 00:58:03,567
Very scared.
Please open the door, son.

719
00:58:03,692 --> 00:58:05,819
Michael, open the door,
or I'll kill you!

720
00:58:05,944 --> 00:58:08,655
That's the way to keep him calm!

721
00:58:08,780 --> 00:58:12,159
Everybody gets scared now and then,
but you can't let it stop you!

722
00:58:12,284 --> 00:58:15,412
You think you're scared now,
wait till the zombies come out!

723
00:58:15,495 --> 00:58:17,247
What zombies?

724
00:58:17,372 --> 00:58:20,667
Just open the door.
We're running out of time!

725
00:58:20,792 --> 00:58:23,629
- Dad, they're coming!
- Open the door!

726
00:58:23,754 --> 00:58:27,382
Michael, open the door now!
Open the door!

727
00:58:30,302 --> 00:58:32,429
Open the door!

728
00:58:41,522 --> 00:58:44,233
Lock it! Lock it!
OK, come on!

729
00:58:46,151 --> 00:58:49,112
OK. All right. Get 'em off.

730
00:58:51,281 --> 00:58:53,158
All right. We got it.
You OK?

731
00:58:53,283 --> 00:58:56,745
All right. OK.
My brave little man.

732
00:58:56,828 --> 00:58:59,331
- All right. You OK?
- You got the key?

733
00:59:04,336 --> 00:59:08,173
Wait. Yeah, I got it.
There it is. OK.

734
00:59:08,340 --> 00:59:12,594
We went to hell and back to get this.
Where's the door out of here?

735
00:59:12,678 --> 00:59:14,805
First, you must find the trunk.

736
00:59:15,514 --> 00:59:17,933
- Trunk?
- Yes, trunk.

737
00:59:18,016 --> 00:59:22,521
- Not door?
- No. Not door. Trunk.

738
00:59:22,646 --> 00:59:24,565
You said I had to find this key.

739
00:59:24,690 --> 00:59:27,150
Now you're telling me
this story about a trunk.

740
00:59:27,234 --> 00:59:29,444
"The key is the answer
to all," remember?

741
00:59:29,528 --> 00:59:31,905
I don't make the rules.
I just work here.

742
00:59:32,030 --> 00:59:35,826
OK, that's the last straw.
I've had enough of this nonsense.

743
00:59:35,951 --> 00:59:38,036
What are you doing?
Put me down!

744
00:59:38,161 --> 00:59:40,497
This is bad luck.
This is very bad luck.

745
00:59:40,622 --> 00:59:43,333
I'll show you bad luck.
I'm tired of playing around.

746
00:59:43,458 --> 00:59:46,086
- I'm getting nauseous!
- You'll get over it.

747
00:59:47,004 --> 00:59:50,424
Please don't drop me.
I'm very fragile.

748
00:59:50,549 --> 00:59:52,551
Don't talk to me about being fragile.

749
00:59:52,676 --> 00:59:55,095
I'm the one that's feeling
fragile right now.

750
00:59:58,223 --> 01:00:00,893
- Is that it?
- That's it.

751
01:00:01,018 --> 01:00:03,061
Now we're in business.

752
01:00:04,563 --> 01:00:06,356
Hold her for a second.

753
01:00:08,650 --> 01:00:10,986
All right. OK.

754
01:00:27,669 --> 01:00:30,464
How do I know what to look for?
It's full of junk.

755
01:00:30,589 --> 01:00:32,758
Find the thing
that must be read.

756
01:00:33,550 --> 01:00:36,136
Lest your heart
be filled with dread.

757
01:00:36,261 --> 01:00:38,555
There's nothing in here red.

758
01:00:41,767 --> 01:00:44,269
Wait a minute.
There's a letter here.

759
01:00:44,394 --> 01:00:46,897
It's a letter.

760
01:00:48,482 --> 01:00:50,901
"Yes, my dear heart,
I will marry you.

761
01:00:51,026 --> 01:00:54,238
I will love you for all eternity,
and tonight, at last,

762
01:00:54,363 --> 01:00:55,822
we will be together.

763
01:00:55,948 --> 01:00:59,826
I do. Forever yours, Elizabeth."

764
01:00:59,952 --> 01:01:03,413
- She didn't kill herself.
- She wanted to be with him.

765
01:01:03,539 --> 01:01:06,083
Yeah, and somebody gave him
the wrong letter.

766
01:01:06,208 --> 01:01:08,544
Yes. Well done, Mr. Evers.

767
01:01:08,627 --> 01:01:11,088
I must say, I am impressed.

768
01:01:11,213 --> 01:01:14,466
You are more persistent
than I would have ever imagined.

769
01:01:15,467 --> 01:01:17,845
The butler did it?
You gotta be kidding me.

770
01:01:17,970 --> 01:01:21,849
I will deal with you two later.

771
01:01:24,226 --> 01:01:28,981
- Why'd you kill her?
- The master wouldn't listen to reason.

772
01:01:29,106 --> 01:01:32,943
He had everything in the world, and yet
he was willing to throw it all away

773
01:01:33,068 --> 01:01:34,319
for love.

774
01:01:34,444 --> 01:01:37,573
I did tell him it would end badly.

775
01:01:38,115 --> 01:01:41,326
- You're a real cold dude.
- No, Mr. Evers.

776
01:01:41,451 --> 01:01:43,287
I am a rational man.

777
01:01:43,412 --> 01:01:45,914
It was my responsibility
to the house,

778
01:01:45,998 --> 01:01:48,750
my duty, sir,
to see to it that the boy

779
01:01:48,834 --> 01:01:52,212
did not make a foolish error
in judgment.

780
01:01:52,337 --> 01:01:56,508
Running away with that girl
would have destroyed this house.

781
01:01:56,633 --> 01:01:58,969
It would have destroyed everything,

782
01:01:59,094 --> 01:02:02,598
and I could not stand by
and watch it fall to ruin.

783
01:02:02,681 --> 01:02:04,183
Punch his face in, Dad.

784
01:02:04,308 --> 01:02:06,643
But first I'll tell
his master what happened.

785
01:02:06,768 --> 01:02:08,729
He must never know.

786
01:02:08,854 --> 01:02:13,483
Edward and his love will be reunited,
and this curse will be broken.

787
01:02:13,609 --> 01:02:15,027
But that's my wife!

788
01:02:15,152 --> 01:02:17,696
And what she sees in you,
I'll never know.

789
01:02:17,821 --> 01:02:20,073
But that is of little importance now.

790
01:02:20,199 --> 01:02:23,994
The only thing that matters is
that the master's pain must end.

791
01:02:24,077 --> 01:02:26,914
And it will end tonight.

792
01:02:27,039 --> 01:02:31,335
The curse will be broken,
and we can all finally move on.

793
01:02:31,460 --> 01:02:34,171
That's it, man.
Where's my wife?

794
01:02:34,296 --> 01:02:36,798
Getting ready for her wedding,
of course.

795
01:02:36,882 --> 01:02:39,092
He can't marry her.
He's dead, she's not.

796
01:02:39,218 --> 01:02:43,013
True, but that can be
easily corrected.

797
01:02:43,138 --> 01:02:47,392
Life, I'm afraid,
is such a delicate state.

798
01:02:47,518 --> 01:02:50,354
If you put one finger on my wife,
I'll kill you!

799
01:02:53,857 --> 01:02:57,486
How wonderful.
You're going to kill a ghost.

800
01:02:57,569 --> 01:03:00,489
- Leave him alone!
- Stop it!

801
01:03:03,200 --> 01:03:05,285
Let 'em go!

802
01:03:08,747 --> 01:03:11,375
Let my kids out of here,
take me to my wife,

803
01:03:11,458 --> 01:03:13,085
and let us out of here right now!

804
01:03:13,210 --> 01:03:15,629
You want out? Fine.

805
01:03:17,214 --> 01:03:19,299
Let me show you out.

806
01:03:23,428 --> 01:03:25,806
Now, for the last time...

807
01:03:25,931 --> 01:03:27,808
Good night, Mr. Evers.

808
01:04:04,803 --> 01:04:07,014
This house has waited so long

809
01:04:07,139 --> 01:04:10,517
to have its shroud
of darkness lifted.

810
01:04:10,642 --> 01:04:12,644
And tonight,

811
01:04:12,769 --> 01:04:15,564
for the first time in...

812
01:04:15,647 --> 01:04:17,774
so many years,

813
01:04:17,858 --> 01:04:19,818
I believe it may be possible.

814
01:04:19,943 --> 01:04:23,572
The story will finally end differently.

815
01:04:24,448 --> 01:04:26,116
Sara.

816
01:04:26,241 --> 01:04:29,453
Do you believe that love
is about second chances?

817
01:04:29,536 --> 01:04:31,371
About forgiveness?

818
01:04:31,496 --> 01:04:34,041
Yes, I do.

819
01:04:35,292 --> 01:04:38,295
- Don't you remember?
- Remember?

820
01:04:38,420 --> 01:04:42,257
- Mr. Gracey, are you all right?
- Don't you recognize me at all?

821
01:04:42,341 --> 01:04:43,759
Mr. Gracey...

822
01:04:43,842 --> 01:04:47,971
I thought bringing you back to
Gracey Manor would help you remember.

823
01:04:48,096 --> 01:04:50,474
Remember what?
Mr. Gracey, you're scaring me.

824
01:04:50,599 --> 01:04:54,478
Where it happened! Where we spent
our last moments together!

825
01:04:54,603 --> 01:04:57,898
Where we danced together
for the last time before you...

826
01:04:58,023 --> 01:05:00,234
before you killed yourself!

827
01:05:00,359 --> 01:05:04,696
Now you've returned to me,
and at long last we can be together!

828
01:05:04,821 --> 01:05:08,158
Why do you not remember?
You're my world, my life,

829
01:05:08,283 --> 01:05:11,078
and I have loved you in death
as I did in life!

830
01:05:11,203 --> 01:05:14,289
- Let me go!
- Why do you not remember?

831
01:05:17,042 --> 01:05:20,254
You are her. You are Elizabeth.
You must be!

832
01:05:20,379 --> 01:05:23,674
Can you not sense it? Search your heart.
I am your one true love.

833
01:05:23,799 --> 01:05:26,635
Now we can finally be together.
Don't you understand?

834
01:05:26,718 --> 01:05:30,305
- Elizabeth, you must listen to me.
- I'm not Elizabeth!

835
01:05:30,389 --> 01:05:34,601
- Please, I implore you!
- Leave me alone. Get away from me!

836
01:05:40,899 --> 01:05:45,279
She doesn't remember.
It can't be her.

837
01:05:45,404 --> 01:05:47,364
It is her, sir.

838
01:05:47,447 --> 01:05:50,951
The Gypsy woman
prophesied her return,

839
01:05:51,076 --> 01:05:54,037
and now the time has come.

840
01:05:54,162 --> 01:05:56,123
You had best get ready.

841
01:05:56,248 --> 01:05:58,125
But she doesn't remember.

842
01:05:58,250 --> 01:06:00,294
In time she will, sir.

843
01:06:00,419 --> 01:06:03,380
I assure you. She will.

844
01:06:09,428 --> 01:06:10,804
Open up!

845
01:06:10,929 --> 01:06:14,558
Hey! Let me in!

846
01:06:47,382 --> 01:06:49,718
Ramsley, you have to help me.

847
01:06:49,801 --> 01:06:51,720
There's something horribly wrong.

848
01:06:51,803 --> 01:06:55,349
- Mr. Gracey...
- Yes, I know, my dear.

849
01:06:55,474 --> 01:06:59,645
He's expecting you.
He's always been expecting you.

850
01:07:00,979 --> 01:07:03,982
And you haven't put on your dress yet.

851
01:07:04,107 --> 01:07:06,443
We can't keep the master waiting.

852
01:07:06,568 --> 01:07:08,487
Waiting? For what?

853
01:07:08,612 --> 01:07:11,490
Why, your wedding, of course.

854
01:07:12,157 --> 01:07:15,285
My... I'm not Elizabeth!

855
01:07:15,410 --> 01:07:17,496
Of course you are, my dear.

856
01:07:17,621 --> 01:07:21,166
You may not see it yet,
but in time you will.

857
01:07:21,291 --> 01:07:24,545
You don't actually think I'm
going through with this madness?

858
01:07:24,670 --> 01:07:27,589
Yes, I very much do.

859
01:07:27,673 --> 01:07:31,969
You see, we wouldn't want
anything to happen

860
01:07:32,052 --> 01:07:34,471
to the children, now, would we?

861
01:07:34,596 --> 01:07:37,307
- Mom! Dad!
- Michael! Megan!

862
01:07:37,432 --> 01:07:40,644
- You wouldn't!
- Of course not, my dear.

863
01:07:40,727 --> 01:07:42,813
But that is entirely up to you.

864
01:07:42,938 --> 01:07:48,735
If not... I really do fear
for the children.

865
01:07:52,614 --> 01:07:54,324
Have her ready.

866
01:07:54,449 --> 01:07:57,953
And this time, any further
acts of insubordination

867
01:07:58,036 --> 01:08:00,789
will be dealt with
in the harshest possible manner.

868
01:08:00,873 --> 01:08:02,624
But, sir...

869
01:08:02,708 --> 01:08:05,878
There are worse things
than purgatory, Madame.

870
01:08:06,003 --> 01:08:07,713
I can assure you.

871
01:08:11,675 --> 01:08:13,510
Have her ready.

872
01:08:56,470 --> 01:08:58,930
Tears of joy.

873
01:09:23,497 --> 01:09:27,459
- What are you doing?
- Hey, you leave me alone.

874
01:09:27,584 --> 01:09:29,336
Get out of here
and leave me alone.

875
01:09:29,461 --> 01:09:33,173
I see. You're gonna sit there
feeling sorry for yourself.

876
01:09:33,298 --> 01:09:37,301
You tell me why not.
This whole thing was my fault.

877
01:09:37,426 --> 01:09:40,596
We shouldn't have
been here in the first place.

878
01:09:40,680 --> 01:09:42,683
We were supposed to be at the lake.

879
01:09:42,808 --> 01:09:44,935
We'd be sitting
by a warm fire right now.

880
01:09:46,270 --> 01:09:48,772
I made us come here.

881
01:09:48,856 --> 01:09:51,524
And now it's too late.

882
01:09:51,649 --> 01:09:54,486
No, it's never too late.

883
01:09:54,611 --> 01:09:57,155
I tried to get in there, and I can't.

884
01:09:57,281 --> 01:10:00,742
- I tried. I failed.
- You try, you fail.

885
01:10:00,826 --> 01:10:02,578
You try, you fail.

886
01:10:02,661 --> 01:10:06,540
But the only true failure
is when you stop trying.

887
01:10:06,665 --> 01:10:09,960
What do you want me to do?

888
01:10:11,670 --> 01:10:13,839
Try again.

889
01:10:20,179 --> 01:10:22,806
- Hold on!
- With what?

890
01:10:35,027 --> 01:10:36,445
Elizabeth?

891
01:10:40,908 --> 01:10:42,743
Yes, my love.

892
01:10:49,541 --> 01:10:53,504
- I'll be right back.
- OK. I'll wait here.

893
01:10:56,215 --> 01:10:57,841
Dearly beloved,

894
01:10:57,966 --> 01:11:00,511
we are gathered together here
in the sight of God

895
01:11:00,636 --> 01:11:04,097
to join this man and this woman
in the bonds of holy matrimony.

896
01:11:09,353 --> 01:11:11,146
Michael! Megan!

897
01:11:15,025 --> 01:11:17,277
Wilt thou, Edward Gracey,

898
01:11:17,402 --> 01:11:20,030
have this woman
to be thy wedded wife,

899
01:11:20,155 --> 01:11:24,910
to live together after God's ordinance
in the holy estate of matrimony?

900
01:11:25,035 --> 01:11:26,245
I will.

901
01:11:30,249 --> 01:11:32,042
And do you,

902
01:11:32,125 --> 01:11:34,044
Elizabeth Henshaw,

903
01:11:34,127 --> 01:11:36,713
take this man to be
your lawful husband,

904
01:11:36,839 --> 01:11:41,009
to love and cherish in death
as you did in life?

905
01:11:42,261 --> 01:11:43,262
I do.

906
01:11:54,147 --> 01:11:55,941
From this day forward,

907
01:11:56,066 --> 01:11:59,570
you shall be joined together
as one for all eternity,

908
01:11:59,653 --> 01:12:02,531
until the very end of time.

909
01:12:06,702 --> 01:12:09,663
Imbibo ut vestri posterus.

910
01:12:09,788 --> 01:12:12,416
What God has joined together,

911
01:12:12,541 --> 01:12:14,835
let no man cast asunder.

912
01:12:18,964 --> 01:12:20,257
Dad!

913
01:12:22,259 --> 01:12:25,429
If anyone has any objections...

914
01:12:28,223 --> 01:12:30,017
Yeah, I got a few objections!

915
01:12:36,815 --> 01:12:40,110
Next time I say we're going to the lake,
we're going to the lake.

916
01:12:40,194 --> 01:12:42,070
Let's go.

917
01:12:42,154 --> 01:12:44,239
Get away from her.

918
01:12:44,323 --> 01:12:48,118
I lost her once. I don't intend
to let it happen again.

919
01:12:48,243 --> 01:12:51,038
This is not Elizabeth.
Ramsley, tell him the truth.

920
01:12:51,163 --> 01:12:53,832
I don't know
what you're talking about.

921
01:12:53,957 --> 01:12:55,083
Now you got amnesia?

922
01:12:55,167 --> 01:12:58,795
Elizabeth didn't kill herself.
He did it. He's lied to you all along.

923
01:12:58,921 --> 01:13:03,634
- I'm warning you, sir. Step away.
- Just 'cause you pull out your sword,

924
01:13:03,717 --> 01:13:07,471
- I'm not gonna let you marry my wife.
- My patience is wearing thin.

925
01:13:07,596 --> 01:13:11,308
- Elizabeth, please, come along.
- I'm not Elizabeth.

926
01:13:11,433 --> 01:13:15,729
- You must be!
- She's Sara from New Jersey.

927
01:13:15,854 --> 01:13:19,733
Ramsley wants you to think
she's Elizabeth to lift this curse.

928
01:13:19,858 --> 01:13:21,652
That is absurd.

929
01:13:21,777 --> 01:13:22,945
Forgive me.

930
01:13:23,028 --> 01:13:26,114
You gonna kill me, kill me.
But when I come on the other side,

931
01:13:26,198 --> 01:13:28,367
I'm gonna whip your ass
for all eternity.

932
01:13:28,492 --> 01:13:30,744
Read this before you stab somebody.

933
01:13:30,869 --> 01:13:32,913
- What is it?
- Elizabeth's letter.

934
01:13:33,038 --> 01:13:36,542
The real letter she wrote.
The one he stole. You never saw it.

935
01:13:45,008 --> 01:13:47,010
What's the meaning of this?

936
01:13:47,135 --> 01:13:51,890
Must we continue to listen
to the ramblings of a lunatic?

937
01:13:52,015 --> 01:13:55,352
- But it is written in her hand.
- Yeah, it's written in her hand.

938
01:13:55,435 --> 01:13:57,312
- Explain that.
- Well?

939
01:14:02,234 --> 01:14:05,279
Your union was unacceptable.

940
01:14:05,404 --> 01:14:09,700
I tried to warn you,
but you wouldn't listen.

941
01:14:09,825 --> 01:14:11,368
So you killed her.

942
01:14:11,451 --> 01:14:15,289
I told you it would be a mistake
to run away with that girl.

943
01:14:15,414 --> 01:14:18,709
But I loved her!
Was love my mistake?

944
01:14:18,834 --> 01:14:20,419
Yes!

945
01:14:20,544 --> 01:14:23,005
I tried to protect you.

946
01:14:23,088 --> 01:14:26,592
All these years,
I've sacrificed for you.

947
01:14:26,717 --> 01:14:31,388
But what would you understand
of sacrifice, duty or honor?

948
01:14:31,513 --> 01:14:33,473
You loved her?

949
01:14:33,599 --> 01:14:35,267
Well, damn you!

950
01:14:35,392 --> 01:14:37,936
Damn you all to hell!

951
01:15:23,565 --> 01:15:24,650
Jim!

952
01:15:59,142 --> 01:16:00,519
Mom!

953
01:16:00,644 --> 01:16:03,480
- Mom, what's wrong?
- Are you all right?

954
01:16:03,605 --> 01:16:07,359
Hey! Hey, Sara, what's the matter?

955
01:16:07,484 --> 01:16:09,528
Sara, what's wrong?

956
01:16:09,653 --> 01:16:11,154
What's wrong?

957
01:16:11,238 --> 01:16:14,283
- It's the poison!
- Oh, no.

958
01:16:14,366 --> 01:16:17,953
No. Hey, Sara?
Please, don't do this.

959
01:16:18,036 --> 01:16:21,790
- Don't do this, please.
- Jim.

960
01:16:23,000 --> 01:16:24,710
Sarah! Hey!

961
01:16:24,835 --> 01:16:27,004
Sara, come on, please.

962
01:16:27,129 --> 01:16:29,673
Sara, I love you.

963
01:16:30,799 --> 01:16:32,676
Sara, please, I love you so much.

964
01:16:40,893 --> 01:16:44,980
- Get away! Leave us alone!
- No, Dad, it won't hurt us.

965
01:17:54,132 --> 01:17:56,301
Elizabeth, is that you?

966
01:17:56,426 --> 01:17:59,221
Yes, my love.

967
01:17:59,304 --> 01:18:02,266
The ghost ball was Elizabeth.

968
01:18:02,391 --> 01:18:05,727
The truth had to be known
for me to be released.

969
01:18:05,811 --> 01:18:07,688
He saved me.

970
01:18:10,274 --> 01:18:12,359
It was nothing.

971
01:18:12,484 --> 01:18:14,236
Oh, Elizabeth.

972
01:18:14,319 --> 01:18:17,865
Yes, my darling?

973
01:18:17,990 --> 01:18:21,827
I have waited so long
for this moment.

974
01:18:21,952 --> 01:18:25,122
And now only heaven awaits.

975
01:18:36,300 --> 01:18:39,595
He's not really kissing your mom.

976
01:18:46,685 --> 01:18:48,645
That's my wife.

977
01:18:56,778 --> 01:18:57,988
Sara?

978
01:19:05,120 --> 01:19:06,496
Jim?

979
01:19:06,622 --> 01:19:09,082
Thought I lost you.

980
01:19:11,502 --> 01:19:14,213
I thought I lost you, too.

981
01:19:14,338 --> 01:19:16,673
I'm back, Sara.

982
01:19:16,757 --> 01:19:19,092
I'm back.

983
01:19:20,928 --> 01:19:22,596
Can you ever forgive me?

984
01:19:22,721 --> 01:19:26,183
What's to forgive? You loved her.

985
01:19:26,517 --> 01:19:29,144
Here. Take this.

986
01:19:30,187 --> 01:19:32,564
- What is it?
- The deed to the house.

987
01:19:32,689 --> 01:19:35,859
It's yours.
Do with it what you will.

988
01:19:35,984 --> 01:19:40,948
Sell it. Keep it. Do whatever
makes you and your family happy.

989
01:19:46,912 --> 01:19:48,539
And thank you.

990
01:19:50,415 --> 01:19:53,544
Thank you all so much.

991
01:20:03,178 --> 01:20:05,055
Wait! Wait for us!

992
01:20:05,180 --> 01:20:07,724
Hold on!

993
01:20:07,850 --> 01:20:10,561
- What's all this?
- I don't know what we'll need.

994
01:20:10,686 --> 01:20:14,064
We're going to heaven.
You can't take it with you.

995
01:20:14,189 --> 01:20:15,566
The hell I can't.

996
01:20:16,692 --> 01:20:17,651
Goodbye.

997
01:20:17,776 --> 01:20:19,570
- Bye-bye.
- Thank you all so much.

998
01:20:19,695 --> 01:20:21,238
- Bye.
- Thank you.

999
01:20:23,615 --> 01:20:25,742
Hurry. Let's go!

1000
01:20:25,868 --> 01:20:28,912
- Bye!
- OK, here we go.

1001
01:20:35,210 --> 01:20:36,712
Bye-bye.

1002
01:20:57,524 --> 01:21:00,485
Angels in heaven,
together at last

1003
01:21:00,611 --> 01:21:03,947
The tale is well-ended
for those who have passed

1004
01:21:04,072 --> 01:21:07,826
Love endures all,
no reason, no rhyme

1005
01:21:07,951 --> 01:21:11,788
It lasts forever
and forever all time

1006
01:21:11,872 --> 01:21:14,124
- Mom, Leota won't shut up.
- Are we there yet?

1007
01:21:14,208 --> 01:21:16,460
- I'm getting hungry.
- Can we get some pizza?

1008
01:21:16,543 --> 01:21:18,128
How long before we get there?

1009
01:21:18,212 --> 01:21:21,715
- 20 minutes, tops.
- Nothing takes 20 minutes.

1010
01:21:25,511 --> 01:21:27,638
Hey, guys, keep it down!

1011
01:21:27,721 --> 01:21:30,307
We'll keep it down
We'll keep it down

1012
01:21:30,390 --> 01:21:34,311
Oh yes, we will
We'll keep it down

1013
01:21:34,436 --> 01:21:37,648
Oh, we're driving
Down the highway

1014
01:21:37,731 --> 01:21:39,816
Yeah

1015
01:21:39,900 --> 01:21:44,154
And we're trying to keep it

1016
01:21:44,238 --> 01:21:46,990
Down

1017
01:27:21,867 --> 01:27:23,827
Hurry back.

1018
01:27:24,494 --> 01:27:27,623
Hurry back!

1019
01:27:27,706 --> 01:27:31,835
Be sure to bring
your death certificate.

1020
01:27:31,960 --> 01:27:34,129
If you decide to join us,

1021
01:27:34,213 --> 01:27:37,549
make your final arrangements now.

1022
01:27:37,633 --> 01:27:41,845
We've been dying to have you.
